<section>
  <p class="kicker"><%= link_to_page "guides", label_type: :nav, class: "cta" %></p>
  <h1>Bravo, one button and a light.</h1>
  <p class="lede">skyBlip Bravo warns you of approaching ADS-B traffic and sends it to your navigation app. Bravo only receives. It does not transmit your position.</p>
</section>

<section>
  <h2 class="kicker">In your hand</h2>

  <div class="feature">
    <div>
      <h3 id="controls">Press to answer, <span class="highlight">hold to switch off</span>.</h3>
      <p>Bravo is a Seeed SenseCAP MeshTracker X1 running skyBlip. Its round button is on the top face. The USB-C port is on a short edge. There is no screen. The LED above the button, a buzzer and a vibration motor tell you what is happening.</p>
    </div>
    <%= render "shared/device", device: :bravo, label: "skyBlip Bravo on a Seeed SenseCAP MeshTracker X1, with its button, the LED just above the button and its USB-C port marked", marks: { button: t("devices.button"), led: t("devices.led"), usb: t("devices.usb") }, caption: "The X1 running skyBlip Bravo. Photo Seeed Studio." %>
  </div>

  <div class="table-scroll">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Gesture</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><th>Press from off</th><td>Switches on, with one green pulse you feel.</td></tr>
        <tr><th>Press during a fast red flicker</th><td>Silences the alarm, including the paired Go while they are linked.</td></tr>
        <tr><th>Press during a fast green blink</th><td>Allows a setting or update requested by a phone or Briefing. Without a press, it expires after 30 seconds.</td></tr>
        <tr><th>Press during a fast blue blink</th><td>Pairs with the Go that asked.</td></tr>
        <tr><th>Hold for 2&nbsp;s</th><td>Switches off, with three red pulses you feel.</td></tr>
        <tr><th>Hold, plug in USB-C, keep holding</th><td>After about 3 seconds, the LED above the button turns white. The X1 becomes a USB drive named X1 for installing firmware by hand. Briefing asks only if it cannot restart Bravo itself.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <p>A press begun before a request arrives answers nothing. A hold never answers a request. The browser that installed Bravo changes settings, updates it and pairs it without a press. Other browsers ask.</p>

  <div class="feature">
    <div>
      <h3 id="light">The colour gives the state, <span class="highlight">the rhythm gives the detail</span>.</h3>
      <p>Blue means no satellite position yet. Green means Bravo knows where it is.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="table-scroll">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Light</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><th><span class="lamp lamp--dot lamp--green" aria-hidden="true"></span> One green pulse, felt</th><td>Just switched on.</td></tr>
        <tr><th><span class="lamp lamp--dot lamp--blue" aria-hidden="true"></span> Blue, every 3&nbsp;s</th><td>No position yet.</td></tr>
        <tr><th><span class="lamp lamp--dot lamp--green" aria-hidden="true"></span> Green, every 3&nbsp;s</th><td>Position found.</td></tr>
        <tr><th><span class="lamp lamp--dot lamp--green" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="lamp lamp--dot lamp--blue" aria-hidden="true"></span> Either colour, every 1.5&nbsp;s</th><td>A phone or Briefing is connected.</td></tr>
        <tr><th><span class="lamp lamp--dot lamp--red" aria-hidden="true"></span> Red, fast flicker</th><td>Traffic alarm.</td></tr>
        <tr><th><span class="lamp lamp--dot lamp--green" aria-hidden="true"></span> Green, fast blink</th><td>A request awaits your press.</td></tr>
        <tr><th><span class="lamp lamp--dot lamp--blue" aria-hidden="true"></span> Blue, fast blink</th><td>A Go asks to pair.</td></tr>
        <tr><th><span class="lamp lamp--dot lamp--green" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="lamp lamp--dot lamp--blue" aria-hidden="true"></span> Two winks every 3&nbsp;s</th><td>A diagnostic recording is armed. The colour still shows the position state.</td></tr>
        <tr><th><span class="lamp lamp--dot lamp--red" aria-hidden="true"></span> Red, every 3&nbsp;s</th><td>Battery low.</td></tr>
        <tr><th><span class="lamp lamp--dot lamp--red" aria-hidden="true"></span> Red, every 600&nbsp;ms</th><td>Battery critical. With a full battery, a traffic or satellite receiver is not answering and Bravo refuses to run.</td></tr>
        <tr><th><span class="lamp lamp--dot lamp--red" aria-hidden="true"></span> Three red pulses, felt</th><td>Switching off, then dark.</td></tr>
        <tr><th>Dark</th><td>Off.</td></tr>
        <tr><th><span class="lamp lamp--dot lamp--white" aria-hidden="true"></span> Steady white</th><td>The X1 is a USB drive for installing firmware.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band band--tint">
  <h2 class="section-title">Before you set off</h2>
  <p>Switch on Bravo in the open. When the light flashes green, Bravo knows its position. With Bravo on its own, connect your compatible navigation app over Bluetooth. With Tango, check on Go's radar that Bravo is connected. ADS-B traffic then appears on Go. It shows the positions that equipped aircraft transmit by radio.</p>
  <p>If your own transponder shows up as another aircraft, <%= link_to_page "install", label: "check its address on the ground", anchor: "si-quelque-chose-bloque" %>.</p>
</section>

<section class="band">
  <h2 class="section-title">After the flight</h2>
  <p>Hold the button for two seconds to switch Bravo off. To update it, switch it back on and open its page in <%= link_to "Briefing", briefing_root_path %>. Follow the instructions on screen.</p>
</section>

